@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Secret-flow and missing access-guard composition

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #495057
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F1F3F5
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "CodePropertyGraph\ntyped AST · CFG · DFG · PDG · calls" as CPG #DBE4FF

package "J3 · secret and credential flow" #F8F9FA {
  component "SecretRuleSet\nsinks · positions · name hints" as SRULE #FFE8CC
  component "literal qualifier\nShannon entropy OR typed binding hint" as QUAL #E5DBFF
  component "shared IFDS taint\nall string origins → security sinks" as TAINT #FFF3BF
  component "flow filter\nqualified origin + governed argument" as SFILTER #74C0FC
  component "SecretAnalysis\nfindings · taint · issues" as SREPORT #D3F9D8
}

package "J4 · missing authentication/authorization" #F8F9FA {
  component "AuthzRuleSet\nmutations · access-guard patterns" as ARULE #FFE8CC
  component "shared missing-check engine\nAPI populations · exact support" as POP #C3FAE8
  component "flat fingerprint filter\ntyped authN/authZ call or member" as AFILTER #74C0FC
  component "AuthzAnalysis\nfindings · analyzed sites · issues" as AREPORT #D3F9D8
}

component "typed incompleteness\npolicy · graph · cap · delegated" as ISSUE #FCC2D7

CPG --> QUAL : typed literals + binding context
SRULE --> QUAL : thresholds + hints
CPG --> TAINT : AST + DFG + calls + summaries
SRULE --> TAINT : categorical strings + sink catalog
QUAL --> SFILTER : qualified literal NodeIds
TAINT --> SFILTER : canonical flow witnesses
SRULE --> SFILTER : governed positions
SFILTER --> SREPORT
QUAL --> ISSUE : literal/context caps
TAINT --> ISSUE : delegated cap/issues

CPG --> POP : calls + AST + PDG + call graph
ARULE --> POP : mutation sink catalog + peer policy
POP --> AFILTER : normalized missing fingerprints
ARULE --> AFILTER : access-guard patterns
AFILTER --> AREPORT
POP --> ISSUE : structural/cap issues
ARULE --> ISSUE : invalid patterns
ISSUE --> SREPORT
ISSUE --> AREPORT

note bottom of CPG
  Both analyses are read-only. Typed graph evidence is
  consumed directly; neither branch reparses source text.
end note

note bottom of SREPORT
  Literal contents are omitted from findings.
  A negative claim requires is_complete() = true.
end note

note bottom of AREPORT
  Population convention is advisory, not an authorization proof.
  A negative claim requires is_complete() = true.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| normalized CPG evidence |
|<#FFE8CC>| caller-owned declarative policy |
|<#E5DBFF>| explicit stack-safe qualification machine |
|<#FFF3BF>| shared taint/data-flow semantics |
|<#C3FAE8>| shared exact population inference |
|<#74C0FC>| detector-specific typed filtering |
|<#D3F9D8>| immutable advisory report |
|<#FCC2D7>| incomplete or invalid evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
